GT patch 0053 (NOT applied: no gain, see FINDINGS 2026-10-20): static quad strips live in a vertex arena on the GPU (docs/superpowers/specs/
2026-10-20-ge-static-strip-arena-design.md). A fast-path strip is keyed by vertex address, count and type; when the
bytes it is decoded from (and the material colour, for types without vertex colour) and its texture level selection
equal the recorded ones, its draw reuses the arena vertices recorded the first time: no decode, no vertex append, no
vertex copy per frame. The geometry buffer starts with the arena (600,000 vertices, copied to the GPU only where new);
a full arena is emptied at the end of a frame. GT_GE_ARENA_VERIFY=1 decodes every hit too and compares it with the
arena copy; GT_GE_ARENA_SABOTAGE=1|2 (a moved vertex, a skipped byte compare) must be reported; GT_GE_NO_ARENA=1 turns
it off.

